/-!
# Condition (2) of the proof of Stacks 0FEW is local around the generic point

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project. The proof of
Proposition 0FEW reduces the proposition to two conditions on the composition
`K'_0(X) ⟶ CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. The second asks that for an integral closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` of
`δ`-dimension `k` the degree `k` part of the image of `[𝒪_Z]` be `[Z]`; the source writes that
image as `(Z ⟶ X)_*` of `ch(Z ⟶ Y, 𝒪_Z[0]) ∩ [Y] ∈ CH_*(Z) ⊗ 𝐐` and argues:

> Since `CH_k(Z) = 𝐙`, in order to prove this we may replace `Y` by an open neighbourhood of the
> generic point `ξ` of `Z`. Since the maximal ideal of the regular local ring `𝒪_{Y, ξ}` is
> generated by a regular sequence (Stacks 00NQ) we may assume the ideal of `Z` is generated by a
> regular sequence (Stacks 063I). Thus we deduce the result from Lemma 0FEH.

This file carries out the first two sentences.

* **The neighbourhood.** If `Y` is regular and `ξ ∈ Y`, the integral closed subscheme `Z_ξ` with
  generic point `ξ` is cut out, over some affine open neighbourhood `V` of `ξ`, by a regular
  sequence of length `r = dim 𝒪_{Y, ξ}`: a minimal set of generators of the maximal ideal of
  `𝒪_{Y, ξ}`, which is the ideal of `Z_ξ` there, is a regular sequence (Stacks 00NQ), and it
  spreads out to a neighbourhood (Stacks 063I).
* **`CH_k(Z) = 𝐙`.** On a scheme `W` of `δ`-dimension at most `k` no `k`-cycle is rationally
  equivalent to zero, so restricting `CH_k(W) ⊗ 𝐐` to an open containing every point of
  `δ`-dimension `k` is injective. For `W = Z` integral of `δ`-dimension `k` the only such point is
  the generic point.
* **Bivariant classes and restriction.** For classes `c_p ∈ A^p(Z ⟶ Y)` and rationals `q_p`, the
  degree `k` part of `∑_p q_p (c_p ∩ [T])` on a test scheme `T ⟶ Y` restricts, along an open
  `T' ⊆ T`, to the same expression for `T'` (Stacks 0B76 (2) and `[T]|_{T'} = [T']`). Hence if the
  degree `k` part of `∑_p q_p (c_p ∩ [V])` is `[Z ×_Y V]`, the degree `k` part of
  `∑_p q_p (c_p ∩ [Y])` is `[Z]`. With Stacks 0FB3 this applies to the localized Chern character
  `ch(Z ⟶ Y, E) = ∑_p P_p(Z ⟶ Y, E)/p!` of Stacks 0FB5 and its base change to `V`.
* **The map `α ↦ ch(α) ∩ [X]`.** For `X` regular Noetherian with affine diagonal (the map of
  Stacks 0FEY, which is that of Stacks 0FEW for `X = Y` by Remark 0FEU), the degree `k` part of
  the image of `[𝒪_{Z_ξ}]` is the pushforward of the degree `k` part of
  `ch(Z_ξ ⟶ X, 𝒪_{Z_ξ}[0]) ∩ [X]`, so condition (2) follows from its local form at every point.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.capFundamentalClassDegreePart` — the degree `k` part of `∑_p q_p (c_p ∩ [T])`.
* `Stacks.Chow.LocalizedSituation.HasFundamentalDegreePart` — in Situation 0GUJ, the degree
  `k` part of `ch(Z ⟶ X, E) ∩ [X]` is `[Z]`.
* `Stacks.Chow.integralComponentLocalizedSituation` — Situation 0GUJ for a perfect object
  isomorphic to `𝒪_{Z_ξ}[0]`.
* `Stacks.Chow.IsDiagonalOnIntegralNear` — the local form of condition (2) at a point.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.exists_isAffineOpen_isRegularClosedImmersionOfCodim_integralComponentAt` — on a
  regular `Y`, `Z_ξ ∩ V ⟶ V` is a regular closed immersion of codimension `dim 𝒪_{Y, ξ}` for an
  affine open `V ∋ ξ`.
* `Stacks.Chow.injective_lTensor_chowGroupRestrict` — `CH_k(W) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_k(U) ⊗ 𝐐` is injective
  when `dim_δ W ≤ k` and `U` contains the points of `δ`-dimension `k`.
* `Stacks.Chow.capFundamentalClassDegreePart_id_eq_of_opens` — the reduction to an open
  neighbourhood, for any family of bivariant classes.
* `Stacks.Chow.LocalizedSituation.hasFundamentalDegreePart_of_pullback` — the same for the
  localized Chern character, from the base-changed situation over the neighbourhood.
* `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCapFundamentalClass_apply_eq_lTensor` — the degree `k` part of
  `ch(α) ∩ [X]` as a pushforward of localized classes.
* `Stacks.Chow.isDiagonalOnIntegral_coherentChernCharacterCapFundamentalClass_of_near` —
  condition (2) for `α ↦ ch(α) ∩ [X]` from its local form at every point.

## Implementation notes

The source computes in `CH_*(Z) ⊗ 𝐐` and only then pushes forward to `X`; the reduction is
carried out there, and must be: `CH_k(Z ∩ V) ⟶ CH_k(V)` need not be injective, so the class of
`[Z ∩ V]` in `CH_k(V) ⊗ 𝐐` (where it may vanish, for instance for a closed point of an affine
curve) does not determine `[Z]` in `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. The classes `c_p ∩ [T]` live in
`CH_{k+p-p}(Z ×_Y T)`, read in degree `k` by `Stacks.Chow.chowGroupDegreeEquiv`, and `Z ×_Y Y` is
the fibre product, identified with `Z` only at the end.

The map `α ↦ ch(α) ∩ [X]` is a sum over the degrees `p` up to a bound read off `δ_{X/S}`, so its
reduction assumes `δ_{X/S}` bounded below, as Stacks 0FEY does; the local hypothesis is asked for
every range `p ≤ N` that is large enough for `X`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEY)
